<node id="&quot;TRANCHE&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COMMITMENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A portion or segment of a loan that is distributed to the borrower based on specific conditions or timelines."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tranche refers to a portion of the loan or financing within the credit agreement, often characterized by distinct terms or conditions."&lt;SEP&gt;"Tranche refers to a portion, piece, or slice of a pool or security, commonly seen in loan arrangements to manage risk."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-0a4b11d9d570dfb94869367bf658bbf44c8a288c83406b056f2db68067634598&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f8ac583fbb163821277a58e5520f364c8b7ff6b8b1cac5c5f9ecaec9187807f6&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-75f1263fe25efcf5e1a778c55ad14ee6ff940f9a9148c8f1d0c8dff83e78bab7</data>
