<node id="&quot;SEC&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"The SEC (Securities and Exchange Commission) is a regulatory body that may require approvals concerning the Scheme and the transactions described in the credit agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SEC is the regulatory body whose approval is necessary before the Borrower can dispatch the Takeover Offer Document."&lt;SEP&gt;"The SEC, or Securities and Exchange Commission, is the regulatory authority that oversees the mutual reporting and compliance obligations of publicly traded companies, including the Borrower."&lt;SEP&gt;"The U.S. Securities and Exchange Commission, responsible for regulating the securities industry and protecting investors."</data>
