</node>
<node id="&quot;LEVEL 4: LESS THAN LEVEL 3 BUT AT LEAST BBB+/BAA1&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"INTEREST RATE"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A rating indicating a higher degree of risk, with an applicable margin of 0.250% to 1.125% in credit agreements."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-c01f63bff235f0de4fd04cc572f42b5048f051f30e90ff46450fed63088a2d1e</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-ef0ff6e2b1ed8219e449e705d6553eb1bc013ea0540e1dcb68482041f8487491</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;MATERIAL ADVERSE EFFECT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"COVENANTS"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A condition that indicates a significant negative impact on a party's financial condition or operations, often invoked in credit agreements to enforce obligations or defaults."&lt;SEP&gt;"A significant negative impact on the borrower's financial condition or operations that might affect repayment capability."&lt;SEP&gt;"A significant negative impact that could affect the borrower's standing or ability to comply with the agreement's terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A term describing a significant negative impact on the business or operations of the Borrower or Consolidated Group, which would affect adherence to agreement terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"A term describing an event that has significant negative consequences on the Borrower's financial condition or operations as outlined in the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"A term used to describe negative impacts on the financial condition or operations of the Borrower, impacting their ability to meet obligations under the agreement."&lt;SEP&gt;"Material Adverse Effect highlights significant changes or events that could impact the Borrower and their ability to adhere to the Agreement terms."&lt;SEP&gt;"Material Adverse Effect refers to a legal standard concerning the impact of compliance failures or operational issues that could adversely affect the Borrower or the transaction."&lt;SEP&gt;"The term Material Adverse Effect identifies conditions that could significantly impact the Borrower's ability to fulfill its obligations under this Agreement."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-f0ed6d0a7062e2fb3635c3defcdbad07963741b071cdc36d7c4b34749a2e718a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-2a55c6b7f04b24ab285d974749d7dffb1b53e9f02ded348a822258c40bd47770&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dece15a26450f3f3b7005a23a1a87b75619c152d1c0c3fb518d24ff11d52843a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-dab0531fa4fcf86f70f5a6e071aafc6b5ff5db2eaa35dfe862105382145767e3&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1583e8d86bec46433cba76eeee6ae8e3d0cee281e57ae7251a6206ddbe83f43&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-8728e39e0e185ee39416c3955fb41ec94d2eef3c5f813cb8b6099f868cf5e02a&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-b8f799d61b01f18934ea147ca074e5f3a01f511964c2cab511d835f90610d21b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-bd2f3c18ca40f5744b1fae1009fdd54117d901009e82d32923eeabad1f6473ae</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-ef0ff6e2b1ed8219e449e705d6553eb1bc013ea0540e1dcb68482041f8487491</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;TAKEOVER RULES&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"REGULATORY"</data>
  <data key="d1">"A set of regulations under which the Takeover Offer and related actions must be conducted."&lt;SEP&gt;"Legislation defined in the Irish Takeover Panel Act 1997, governing the process and requirements of takeovers."&lt;SEP&gt;"The Takeover Rules are regulations that impose restrictions and guidelines for disclosing information related to credit agreements, particularly during the debt syndication process."</data>
  <data key="d2">chunk-1f8d5bdd05b7cd0d1c2d946f291696266d96f16ce4e2c34eb03dcb8cc207d234&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-f1a4b40fb4e1d23fccdbfe49f84af59e707d9fec7e183f7052d6148e7630846b&lt;SEP&gt;chunk-78950c530681eb30ebd5dd748958c0ddb8dd93b84a33af76f5beae6548792ae1</data>
  <data key="d3">DOC-ef0ff6e2b1ed8219e449e705d6553eb1bc013ea0540e1dcb68482041f8487491</data>
</node>
<node id="&quot;BENCHMARK UNAVAILABILITY PERIOD&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"EVENT"</data>
