</node>
<node id="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d0">"AGENT"</data>
  <data key="d1">The "ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT" is a designated entity responsible for managing the administrative and operational aspects of a credit agreement. This entity plays a crucial role in ensuring effective communication and coordination among participants, which typically include lenders and the borrower. The Administrative Agent oversees critical functions such as fund disbursement, the execution and adherence to provisions of the agreement, and the facilitation of communication regarding financial transactions.

In their capacity, the Administrative Agent is tasked with managing the duties and rights under the credit agreement. This includes appointing sub-agents, overseeing compliance with terms, and ensuring all parties comply with the requirements set forth. They are responsible for managing communications related to principal, interest, and fees under the agreement, and they play a vital role in representing the interests of the lenders while coordinating actions among them.

Additionally, the Administrative Agent manages the administrative duties associated with the credit facility, including activities related to agreements on changes or actions impacting the loan structure, such as managing benchmark replacements and spread adjustments. They are also expected to inform parties of any significant developments, including updates on compliance, funding requests, and interest rate adjustments.

Overall, the Administrative Agent serves as a liaison among lenders and the borrower, ensuring that the obligations of the credit agreement are met and facilitating all interactions necessary for the smooth operation of the financial arrangements.</data>
