<edge source="&quot;BORROWER&quot;" target="&quot;LENDER&quot;">
  <data key="d4">240.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The relationship between the BORROWER and the LENDER is governed by a credit agreement that clearly outlines the obligations and interactions between both entities. Each LENDER is responsible for notifying the BORROWER and the Administrative Agent in writing in the event of any legal inability to provide funds. Additionally, each LENDER must identify the BORROWER and any Guarantor in accordance with the requirements of the Patriot Act.

Under the terms specified in the Agreement, the LENDER provides financial support to the BORROWER, establishing a creditor-debtor relationship. The BORROWER receives funds from the LENDER and is legally obligated to repay the loan as per the stipulations detailed in the credit agreement. This includes a responsibility to adhere to repayment obligations and any other terms set forth in the Agreement. The BORROWER's obligation is to ensure all payments are made in accordance with the specified timelines and conditions.

Moreover, the LENDER's provision of funds is contingent upon the BORROWER's compliance with the credit agreement. The commitment and obligations of both parties are essential to maintaining the integrity of the borrowing-lending relationship. The LENDER expects the BORROWER to fulfill these financial responsibilities and adhere to confidentiality requirements regarding the management and repayment processes defined within the Loan Documents.</data>
  <data key="d6">"Financial Obligations"&lt;SEP&gt;"Loan relationship, financing"&lt;SEP&gt;"Provides funds to"&lt;SEP&gt;"borrowing"&lt;SEP&gt;"contractual obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;"financing, obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;"funding responsibility"&lt;SEP&gt;"funding, contract"&lt;SEP&gt;"identification"&lt;SEP&gt;"loan agreement"&lt;SEP&gt;"notify"&lt;SEP&gt;"obligated to, repay"&lt;SEP&gt;"obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;"provide, loan, repayment"&lt;SEP&gt;"provides funding"&lt;SEP&gt;"provides funds"&lt;SEP&gt;"receives funds, repays loan"&lt;SEP&gt;"repayment obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;"repayment"&lt;SEP&gt;"responsibility, obligation"&lt;SEP&gt;10&lt;SEP&gt;9&lt;SEP&gt;financing relationship&lt;SEP&gt;funding, creditor-debtor&lt;SEP&gt;obligatory relationship</data>
