<edge source="&quot;LENDER&quot;" target="&quot;ADMINISTRATIVE AGENT&quot;">
  <data key="d4">158.0</data>
  <data key="d5">The Lender has authorized the Administrative Agent to release all amounts deposited and make those funds available to the Borrower. In this capacity, the Administrative Agent acts on behalf of the Lender in managing various aspects of the credit agreement, including coordinating communication and actions related to the Agreement. This includes overseeing compliance with the terms of the Loan Documents and ensuring that the Borrower adheres to the credit terms and conditions.

The Administrative Agent plays a pivotal role in facilitating the borrowing process and managing the flow of funds, while also coordinating and performing duties on behalf of the Lender. This involves managing commitments to the Borrower, handling logistics surrounding the loan agreement, and facilitating communication between the Lender and the Borrower. The Agent is responsible for the relationship between all parties involved, ensuring effective coordination and compliance with applicable agreements.

Additionally, the Administrative Agent indemnifies the Lender for any taxes attributable to the Lender, oversees compliance with confidentiality restrictions set forth by the Takeover Rules, and ensures that all operations align with regulatory requirements. The relationship between the Lender and the Administrative Agent is built on trust and responsibility, with the latter ensuring that the Lender's interests are upheld throughout the operational and financial processes associated with the credit agreement. Both parties work collaboratively to manage and administer the agreement effectively, addressing tax documentation and reporting needs, while ensuring the successful management of loans and obligations.</data>
